all-MiniLM-L6-v2  —  https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The embedding model memory search runs (payload/model/), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, by its authors (sentence-transformers; the base
model is nreimers/MiniLM-L6-H384-uncased). Shipped unmodified: the upstream
repository's own int8-quantised ONNX export (onnx/model_qint8_arm64.onnx) and
tokenizer.json, at revision 1110a243fdf4706b3f48f1d95db1a4f5529b4d41. The
upstream repository carries no NOTICE file to reproduce.

The runtime that executes it is frozen into payload/runtime/ with the engine:
ONNX Runtime (MIT, Microsoft), Hugging Face tokenizers (Apache-2.0), NumPy
(BSD-3-Clause) and sqlite-vec (MIT or Apache-2.0, Alex Garcia). Their licence
files travel inside their package directories in the payload.

================================================================================
Design references — no code included
================================================================================

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
claude-mem  —  https://github.com/thedotmack/claude-mem  (Apache-2.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Cartograph's memory capability was designed with claude-mem (Copyright 2026
Alex Newman) as its reference: the idea of durable session memory for a coding
agent, and the shape of its query surface.

**No claude-mem code is included in this product.** An earlier draft of this
file claimed portions of `memory/` were derived from it; that was never true,
and the architecture leaves almost nothing to derive — MCP removed, Chroma
replaced by sqlite-vec, its tree-sitter grammars replaced by the engine's
precompiled parser, summarisation shelled out to the host agent.

Apache-2.0 section 4(d) requires reproducing a NOTICE for derivative works.
This is not one, so nothing is reproduced here. The attribution is kept anyway,
because where an idea came from is worth saying. See PROVENANCE.md.
